Body:
- To work around this issue for now, the only option is to modify `~/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc` or the `opencode.jsonc` file within the project. Default values ​​are documented at https://opencode.ai/docs/zh-cn/permissions/#%E9%BB%98%E8%AE%A4%E5%80%BC , and the location of the configuration file is documented at https://opencode.ai/docs/zh-cn/config/#%E4%BC%98%E5%85%88%E7%BA%A7%E9%A1%BA%E5%BA%8F .

```bash
tee ~/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc <<'EOF'
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "permission": {
    "external_directory": {"*": "allow"}
  }
}
EOF
```

- Personally, I am not inclined to change the default values ​​for `doom_loop` and `read`. 
- However, I believe the `opencode web` interface should eventually support more fine-grained permission configurations, similar to how configuration files `opencode.jsonc` work.
